      "content": "I hear the exhaustion in your words, and it is completely valid to feel that you want to stop the pain, but please know that no one can \"fix\" the pain of your loss. Your grief is as real and necessary as the grief you felt dying, and it is okay to carry it even if it feels like you are alone in it. Please consider one last, private conversation with a doctor or a harm-reduction counselor just to talk to someone you trust, because thinking that ending your life is the only way to get peace is a survival reaction, not a solution, and you do not have to carry the world alone.",
